        "audio_url": "https://dcs-cached.megaphone.fm/NSR3654039984.mp3?key=5327c5d64f54bd0a4b2f1d788e104e9c&request_event_id=17796fd2-4b39-443f-8d10-b19031797e5e&session_id=17796fd2-4b39-443f-8d10-b19031797e5e&timetoken=1795711483_79C3A51B9506826E970C18879E82C1B6",
        "description": "In 1095, Pope Urban II made a call to arms that would completely transform the medieval world, setting in motion a wave of crusading zeal that would ripple on for centuries. Promising spiritual reward to those willing to take up the cross and journey east to fight for Jerusalem, his speech resulted in the violent capture of the Holy City and formation of a new world of crusader states.But why did this message resonate so powerfully with the medieval mindset? In this first episode of this four-part series, Emily Briffett and historian Jonathan Phillips explore how this 11th-century call to arms sparked one of history’s most significant religious and military movements. ----- GET MORE WITH MEMBERSHIP Become a HistoryExtra podcast member and unlock access to The Full Story podcast, plus enjoy ad-free listening, early access to other podcast episodes, and a member-exclusive newsletter. Find out more and sign up here: ⁠https://historyextra.supportingcast.fm⁠ ----- EXPLORE MORE For more fascinating stories from the past, head to HistoryExtra, the home of ‘History’s Greatest’ podcasts. Find out more at ⁠⁠⁠historyextra.com/podcast⁠⁠⁠. ----- GET IN TOUCH We'd love to know what you think about the podcast, so leave us a review and let us know the topics you think we should be covering. Or, follow us on ⁠Facebook⁠, ⁠X⁠, ⁠Instagram⁠ or ⁠YouTube⁠ to keep in touch. Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices",
